    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d757">

                <pb facs="0783" n="525" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg525"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2131</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bernstorff</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cedarhurst, N. Y.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 24, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 25.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: After Mr. Chandler Anderson’s visit to me, of which he
                    will have informed you, I thought it advisable to send the enclosed telegram to
                    Berlin. If you agree, I beg you to be good enough to forward it as usual by
                    wireless. Should you, however, wish to speak to me before the telegram goes, I
                    will be at your disposal any moment.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Bernstorff</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d757-a1.xml" xpointer="d757-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
